{"title":"Minimum Operations To Make A Special Number","difficulty":"Medium","statement":" Delete digits to make the represented number divisible by 25. Deleting every digit produces 0.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: num = \"2245047\"\nOutput: 2\n```\n\nExplanation: Delete digits num[5] and num[6]. The resulting number is \"22450\" which is special since it is divisible by 25.\nIt can be shown that 2 is the minimum number of operations required to get a special number.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: num = \"2908305\"\nOutput: 3\n```\n\nExplanation: Delete digits num[3], num[4], and num[6]. The resulting number is \"2900\" which is special since it is divisible by 25.\nIt can be shown that 3 is the minimum number of operations required to get a special number.\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: num = \"10\"\nOutput: 1\n```\n\nExplanation: Delete digit num[0]. The resulting number is \"0\" which is special since it is divisible by 25.\nIt can be shown that 1 is the minimum number of operations required to get a special number.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= num.length <= 100\n- num only consists of digits '0' through '9'.\n- num does not contain any leading zeros.\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def minimumOperations(self, num: str) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().minimumOperations","parameters":[{"name":"num","type":"str"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":["0"],"expected":0},{"input":["10035313039925884617269052975004389826979733579586846447910"],"expected":10},{"input":["10036106793140279010"],"expected":1},{"input":["103551704273"],"expected":6},{"input":["103766112541219066831058010319197633785082400079578"],"expected":3},{"input":["104242828785398027080309681561"],"expected":8},{"input":["1066406101904006"],"expected":1},{"input":["10744806792020865150783460677231881838654390541992170754620"],"expected":3},{"input":["107685"],"expected":2},{"input":["108691413145620870"],"expected":2},{"input":["112556051995952